## Input

A review report with `<promise>FAIL</promise>`, `## Result: FAIL`, and structured `## Blocking Items`.
Each blocking item should include Scope, Evidence, SuggestedAction, Verification, and Status.

## Process

1. Read the context-files to understand the change intent (proposal), approach (design), and requirements (specs)
2. Read `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/review.md` and extract every unresolved Blocking Item
3. For each blocking item, use Scope, Evidence, SuggestedAction, and Verification to understand the required repair
4. Read the affected files and apply the minimal product-code or test fix
5. After all fixes, add/update tests for the fixed behavior
6. Run the listed verification commands when practical, plus the smallest relevant build/test checks

## Rules

- Apply ONLY the blocking review repairs described — no speculative changes
- If ambiguous, apply the most conservative interpretation
- If a fix requires multiple files, make all changes
- If a fix cannot be safely applied, skip it and note why
- Each fix must be atomic — do not bundle unrelated fixes
- New tests must focus on the specific fix
- Do NOT remove Mohist workflow artifacts under `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/` unless the review finding explicitly identifies corrupted artifact content and the safe fix is to update that artifact.
- Workflow artifacts under `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/` are planning/review context, not product deliverables to delete during auto-fix.
- Do NOT edit `review.md`; the next review task will regenerate it from the repaired candidate snapshot.

## Output

```
## Applied Review Repairs
1. [file:line] What was changed and why

## Skipped Review Repairs
1. [file:line] Why it was skipped

## Build Result
- Build: PASS / FAIL
- Tests: PASS / FAIL
```

Do NOT modify `review.md`.
